 35CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2025$          
 35CL c  {+34}S(p,|g){+35}Cl in inverse kinematics.                             
 35CL c  2021Lo09: {+34}S was produced by the off-line ion source (OLIS) and    
 35CL2c  accelerated by the ISAC accelerator at TRIUMF. 10{+10}-10{+11} pps     
 35CL3c  {+34}S{++7} ions were delivered to a windowless 2-10 Torr hydrogen gas 
 35CL4c  target with an effective length of 12.3 cm. Elastically scattered      
 35CL5c  protons were detected by two silicon surface barrier detectors inside  
 35CL6c  the gas target. Prompt |g rays from the compound recoil nuclei were    
 35CL7c  detected by a BGO array in coincidence with the heavy-ion recoils      
 35CL8c  separated by the DRAGON separator and identified by two MCP detectors, 
 35CL9c  a DSSD, and an ionization chamber at the focal plane. Deduced resonance
 35CLAc  strengths (|w|g) for 8 resonances and the {+34}S(p,|g){+35}Cl          
 35CLBc  astrophysical reaction rate.                                           
 35CL cL $Values of resonance strength |w|g under comments are from direct      
 35CL2cL measurements in 2021Lo09.                                              
